---
import Prose from "../layouts/Prose.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPO, SITE_REPO, AUTHOR } from "../consts";

const title = "Contact";
const description =
  "How to report a bug, ask a question, raise a security issue, or correct " +
  "the documentation for Jostraca.";
---

<Prose
  title={title}
  description={description}
  lede="Jostraca is maintained in the open. Every route below is public, and the issue tracker is the one to reach for first."
>
  <h2 id="bugs">Bugs and questions</h2>

  <p>
    Open an issue on
    <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO}/issues`} rel="noopener">the generator's issue tracker</a>.
    That is the primary support channel, and where an answer is most likely,
    because the answer stays where the next person will find it.
  </p>

  <p>
    A good report names the version you are on, whether you are using the
    TypeScript package or the Go module, and the smallest generator that shows
    the problem. Both implementations are held to a shared test corpus, so if
    something differs between them, report it separately. A divergence is a
    bug even when neither side is obviously wrong.
  </p>

  <h2 id="docs">Corrections to this documentation</h2>

  <p>
    The pages on this site are generated from the generator repository, not
    written here, so a correction belongs upstream where the examples are
    executed against the code. Open an issue or a pull request on
    <a href={GITHUB_REPO} rel="noopener">the generator</a> and the fix reaches
    this site on the next sync.
  </p>

  <p>
    Something wrong with the site itself -  a broken link, a rendering problem,
    an accessibility fault -  belongs on
    <a href={SITE_REPO} rel="noopener">the site repository</a> instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Security</h2>

  <p>
    Report a suspected vulnerability privately through
    <a href={`${GITHUB_REPO}/security/advisories/new`} rel="noopener">GitHub's
    private advisory form</a> rather than a public issue, so a fix can be
    prepared before the details are public. Please include the version affected
    and, where you can, a minimal reproduction. You will get an
    acknowledgement; this is a small open source project rather than a company
    with a staffed security desk, so please size your expectations accordingly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="maintainer">The maintainer</h2>

  <p>
    Jostraca is written and maintained by
    <a href={AUTHOR.url} rel="noopener">{AUTHOR.name}</a>. For anything that
    genuinely does not fit a public issue -  a commercial question, a
    conversation you cannot have in the open -  the contact routes on
    <a href={AUTHOR.url} rel="noopener">his site</a> are the way through.
  </p>

  <p class="footnote">
    There is no phone line and no postal desk: this is an open source project,
    and the issue tracker is the answer to "how do I reach you". The
    machine-readable version of this page is
    <a href="/contact.md">/contact.md</a>, and the site's contact point is
    published in the JSON-LD on the <a href="/">home page</a>.
  </p>
</Prose>
